  exact version).
type: software
title: 'CRA-SME Toolkit: a risk-driven, evidence-based research toolkit for EU Cyber Resilience Act implementation
  in SMEs'
version: 1.3.0
date-released: 2026-10-18
license: Apache-2.0
authors:
- family-names: Torstensson
  given-names: Olga
  affiliation: School of Information Technology, Halmstad University, Sweden
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2169-6851
- family-names: Prokopovych-Tkachenko
  given-names: Dmytro
  affiliation: Department of Cybersecurity and Information Technologies, University of Customs and Finance, Dnipro, Ukraine
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6590-3898
abstract: 'Research toolkit for implementing and evaluating the EU Cyber Resilience Act (Regulation (EU)
  2024/2847) in small and medium-sized enterprises. It contains a 46-obligation CRA requirements catalogue,
  a risk and evidence workbook, a tested Python core (release-decision engine, ordinal and Monte Carlo
  risk models, inter-rater agreement statistics, SBOM and scanner accuracy metrics, Article 14 reporting
  clocks, a traceability schema with a score-independent release gate, and an evidence provenance manifest),
  a SHA-pinned CI evidence workflow, protocols for eight experiments (E1-E8), executed Jupyter notebooks,
  and an SBOM generator pilot benchmark. Research instruments only: not legal advice and not a conformity
  assessment.'
keywords:
- Cyber Resilience Act
- Regulation (EU) 2024/2847
- SME
- SBOM
- compliance as code
- cybersecurity risk assessment
- evidence traceability
- vulnerability disclosure
- design science research
